{#- modules/guardrails/semgrep-rule.j2
    A house Semgrep rule: the requirement in one sentence, the YAML that
    enforces it, and the code it catches next to the code it wants.

    Layout follows the AI-Augmented lab deck's "Policy as Code: Semgrep
    Rules" slide. The rule itself is an authorization guardrail for FastAPI
    (/admin routes must carry Depends(require_role("admin")) in the
    signature), checked against positive and negative samples with Semgrep
    1.181 before it went on the slide.

    Written against the brand-pack primitive contract (see AGENTS.md): colours
    come from the engine's --slide-* and --accent-* tokens. Import WITH CONTEXT:

      {%- from "modules/guardrails/semgrep-rule.j2" import house_rule with context %}
-#}

{%- from "modules/branding/" ~ branding ~ "/primitives.j2" import
    content_slide,
    slide_heading
-%}


{%- macro house_rule() -%}
{%- call content_slide("Semgrep rule") %}
  <style>
    .sg { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; margin-top: 10px; }
    .sg-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
    .sg-k { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slide-ink-3); margin: 0; }
    .sg-win { border: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--slide-sunken); overflow: hidden; }
    .sg-win.warn { border-color: var(--accent-warning); }
    .sg-win.bad  { border-color: var(--accent-danger); }
    .sg-win.good { border-color: var(--accent-success); }
    .sg-hdr { padding: 8px 14px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline); color: var(--slide-ink-2); }
    .sg-win.bad  .sg-hdr { color: var(--accent-danger); }
    .sg-win.good .sg-hdr { color: var(--accent-success); }
    .sg-win.warn .sg-hdr { color: var(--accent-warning); }
    .sg-code { margin: 0; padding: 14px 16px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--slide-ink); white-space: pre; }
    .sg-code .c { color: var(--slide-ink-3); }
    .sg-note { font-size: 15px; color: var(--slide-ink-2); margin: 0; }
    .sg-note code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  </style>
  {{ slide_heading("", "Semgrep: pattern-based static analysis",
                   "&ldquo;Every route under /admin requires the admin role, enforced in the route signature, not in the handler&rdquo;") }}
  <div class="sg">
    <div class="sg-col">
      <p class="sg-k">Semgrep rule (YAML)</p>
      <div class="sg-win warn">
        <div class="sg-hdr">admin-route-requires-admin-role.yaml</div>
<pre class="sg-code">rules:
  - id: admin-route-requires-admin-role
    languages: [python]
    severity: ERROR
    patterns:
      - pattern: |
          @$APP.$METHOD($PATH, ...)
          def $FUNC(...):
            ...
      - metavariable-regex:
          metavariable: $METHOD
          regex: ^(get|post|put|patch|delete)$
      - metavariable-regex:
          metavariable: $PATH
          regex: ^["']/admin(/|["'])
      - pattern-not: |
          @$APP.$METHOD($PATH, ...)
          def $FUNC(..., $U = Depends(require_role("admin")), ...):
            ...
      - pattern-not: |
          @$APP.$METHOD($PATH, ..., dependencies=[..., Depends(require_role("admin")), ...], ...)
          def $FUNC(...):
            ...
    message: |
      /admin routes enforce the admin role in the signature,
      where FastAPI runs it before the handler and a reviewer
      can see it. A check inside the body is easy to skip.</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-col">
      <p class="sg-k">Code it catches</p>
      <div class="sg-win bad">
        <div class="sg-hdr">&#x2717; Authenticated, never authorized</div>
<pre class="sg-code">@app.post("/admin/users/{user_id}/roles")
async def set_roles(user_id: str, roles: list[str],
                    user: User = Depends(current_user)):
    return await repo.set_roles(user_id, roles)</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-win good">
        <div class="sg-hdr">&#x2713; Role required before the handler runs</div>
<pre class="sg-code">@app.post("/admin/users/{user_id}/roles")
async def set_roles(user_id: str, roles: list[str],
                    user: User = Depends(require_role("admin"))):
    return await repo.set_roles(user_id, roles)</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="sg-note">Any signed-in user could grant themselves admin. The rule reads the decorator path, the HTTP method, and the parameter list; a check buried in the body does not satisfy it. Verified with Semgrep 1.181: two unguarded <code>/admin</code> routes flagged, three guarded ones and <code>/administrivia</code> passed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endcall %}
{%- endmacro -%}
